## Test Smell Audit — Academic Catalog (testsmells.org)

**Target:** `DataAccess.IntegrationTests/UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`  
**Framework:** MSTest 4.1 (.NET 10)  
**Integration calibration:** Applied — class is annotated `[TestCategory("Integration")]`

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 3           | 3              |
| Medium   | 1           | 1              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4**          |

---

### Findings by Severity

#### 🔴 HIGH — Sleepy Test

**Test:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 87)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000); // ← blocks for 3 seconds with no guarantees
```

Even in integration tests, `Thread.Sleep` introduces non-deterministic timing and slows the suite. The event may arrive sooner or later than 3 s depending on load.

**Fix — use a polling/retry helper or async wait:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var sent = await WaitUntilAsync(
        () => _repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));

    Assert.IsTrue(sent);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky failures under CI load; 3 s tax on every run.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic

**Test:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (lines 101–108)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

One branch is never exercised per run — you don't know which scenario actually ran, creating a hidden testing gap.

**Fix — split into two explicit tests:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenStandard_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenPremium_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    _repository.InsertPremium(new PremiumUser("eve@example.com", "Eve", 0.1m));
    var loaded = (PremiumUser)_repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com")!;
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — one path silently untested.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test)

**Test:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (lines 113–119)

```csharp
for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
{
    _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
}
// No assertion — passes even if inserts silently fail
```

The method name implies a "does not throw" intent, but MSTest will only catch unhandled exceptions. Silent data loss goes undetected.

**Fix — assert the observable outcome:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));

    Assert.AreEqual(100, _repository.ListAll().Count);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False pass — 0% defect-detection ability.

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette

**Test:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (lines 35–38)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

Four assertions with no message parameters. When one fails in CI, the log shows a generic message and a line number but no semantic context.

**Fix — add assertion messages:**

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should roundtrip");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should roundtrip");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Database should assign a positive ID");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slower diagnosis in CI failure logs.

---

### Smell-Free Patterns ✅

The remaining tests are well-structured:

- **`UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord`** and **`DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase`** — clear arrange/act/assert, focused, appropriate for integration scope.
- **`ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted`** — self-documenting count (`3` items added → assert 3), using `CollectionAssert`.
- **`InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity`** — legitimate concurrency integration test with a clear assertion.
- **General Fixture** is clean — both `_connection` and `_repository` are used by every test.
- **No Mystery Guest** — the in-memory SQLite connection is hermetic and test-local.

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix | Effort |
|----------|-------|-----|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | Add `Assert.AreEqual(100, …)` | ~1 min |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | Split into 2 focused tests | ~5 min |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with async poll | ~10 min |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | Add message strings to 4 asserts | ~2 min |

Fixes 1–2 eliminate false-pass risk (highest value). Fix 3 removes flakiness and shaves 3 s off every run. Fix 4 is cosmetic but improves CI diagnostics.
